<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFF8E7">
  <title>Team Group 14 | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (function () {
      try {
        const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
        const preferredTheme = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
        document.documentElement.setAttribute(
          "data-theme",
          savedTheme === "light" || savedTheme === "dark" ? savedTheme : preferredTheme
        );
      } catch (error) {
        document.documentElement.setAttribute(
          "data-theme",
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light"
        );
      }
    }());
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent: #E4007C;
    }

    [data-theme="light"] {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --secondary: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --border: #E8E1D4;
      --soft: #F5EFDF;
      --shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    }

    [data-theme="dark"] {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --secondary: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --border: #383858;
      --soft: #292947;
      --shadow: none;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 0.25rem;
    }

    a:focus-visible,
    button:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 0.25rem;
    }

    .site-header {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .header-inner,
    main,
    .footer-inner {
      width: min(100% - 4rem, 70rem);
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .header-inner {
      min-height: 15rem;
      padding-block: 3rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1,
    h2,
    h3,
    p {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    }

    .tagline {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      max-width: 42rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }

    .header-actions {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .theme-toggle {
      min-height: 2.75rem;
      padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      font-weight: 650;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .theme-toggle:hover {
      background: var(--soft);
    }

    main {
      padding-block: 3rem;
    }

    section + section {
      margin-top: 4rem;
    }

    .section-intro {
      max-width: 48rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    }

    .section-intro p,
    .future-intro {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .member-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .member-photo {
      display: block;
      width: 8rem;
      height: 8rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 50%;
      object-fit: cover;
    }

    .member-card h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .member-background {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .member-details {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .member-details p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .detail-label {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .hot-take {
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
      padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #FFFFFF;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .future-panel {
      padding: 2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .future-intro {
      max-width: 50rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .agreement-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .agreement-grid li {
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--soft);
    }

    .agreement-grid strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .disagreement {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px dashed var(--border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
    }

    .disagreement h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }

    .disagreement p {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .site-footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--secondary);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .footer-inner {
      padding-block: 1.5rem;
    }

    .site-footer p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .header-inner,
      main,
      .footer-inner {
        width: calc(100% - 2rem);
      }

      .header-inner {
        min-height: 0;
        padding-block: 2rem;
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1.5rem;
      }

      .header-actions {
        width: 100%;
        justify-content: space-between;
      }

      main {
        padding-block: 3rem;
      }

      .member-grid,
      .agreement-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .future-panel {
        padding: 1.5rem;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html {
        scroll-behavior: auto;
      }

      body {
        transition: none;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Agentic Software Engineering Lab · Paderborn</p>
        <h1>Group 14</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Five humans, a handful of agents, and an ongoing investigation into who opened all those tabs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <a href="#team">Meet the team</a>
        <button class="theme-toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">
          <span aria-hidden="true">☾</span> <span class="toggle-label">Night mode</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="team" aria-labelledby="team-heading">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">The humans in the loop</p>
        <h2 id="team-heading">Meet Group 14</h2>
        <p>We bring backend, cloud, security, data science, and AI experience to the same table. Our shared workflow: ask the agent, read the diff, run the tests, and then ask why there are 15 tabs open.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="member-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:aryan.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Aryan">
          <h3>Aryan</h3>
          <p class="member-background">M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn University. Previously an Associate Software Engineer at Toddle, building Node.js APIs and production systems, and a research intern at NYCU in Taiwan. B.Sc. Computer Science, Chandigarh University.</p>
          <div class="member-details">
            <p><span class="detail-label">Into</span>Agentic AI, backend systems, and learning German one Artikel at a time.</p>
            <p><span class="detail-label">Off-script</span>At A2 German, Aryan and his coding agent are both still learning to follow instructions.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI won’t replace developers who write tests. It’ll replace the ones who never read its code.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:cemon.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Cemon">
          <h3>Cemon</h3>
          <p class="member-background">M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn University. B.E. Computer Science and Engineering, Dayananda Sagar College of Engineering, Bangalore. 3.5 years of software development experience.</p>
          <div class="member-details">
            <p><span class="detail-label">Into</span>Music and AI concepts.</p>
            <p><span class="detail-label">Off-script</span>One episode turns into 3 a.m. Surprisingly, this is also how debugging starts.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Software engineers will take responsibility for testing code they didn’t write.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:rachana.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Rachana">
          <h3>Rachana</h3>
          <p class="member-background">M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn University. B.E. Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, East West Institute of Technology, Bangalore. Interested in machine learning and data science.</p>
          <div class="member-details">
            <p><span class="detail-label">Into</span>Machine learning, reading, music, and cooking.</p>
            <p><span class="detail-label">Off-script</span>Opens a laptop for one quick task; leaves with 15 tabs and an entirely different task.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI can write a thousand lines in seconds; finding the tiny bug that breaks everything is another story.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:shrividya.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Shrividya">
          <h3>Shrividya</h3>
          <p class="member-background">M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn University. B.E. Information Science and Engineering, Global Academy of Technology, Bengaluru. Experience in cybersecurity, cloud security, DevSecOps, and security automation.</p>
          <div class="member-details">
            <p><span class="detail-label">Into</span>Sketching, basketball, dancing, exploring new places, and trying new technologies.</p>
            <p><span class="detail-label">Off-script</span>Basketball taught her teamwork matters—even when nobody wants to pass the ball.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI can write the code, but it can’t take responsibility when the system breaks at 3 a.m.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:srajan.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Srajan">
          <h3>Srajan</h3>
          <p class="member-background">M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn University. B.E. Computer Science and Engineering, New Horizon College of Engineering, Bangalore. Former AWS Cloud Engineer; now a Werkstudent data scientist at Uniper.</p>
          <div class="member-details">
            <p><span class="detail-label">Into</span>Football, video games, and cloud architecture.</p>
            <p><span class="detail-label">Off-script</span>Can watch a 0–0 draw for 90 minutes and call it tactically fascinating.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 An AI you can’t explain is just a very expensive guess with good formatting.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our shared forecast (with room for revisions)</p>
        <h2 id="future-heading">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
        <p class="future-intro">We don’t think the job disappears. We think the job description gets edited—probably by an agent, then carefully reviewed by a human.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="future-panel">
        <ul class="agreement-grid">
          <li>
            <strong>First drafts get faster.</strong>
            AI is useful for boilerplate, test starting points, refactoring, and exploring possible solutions. That’s a head start, not a correctness certificate.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Clear thinking beats fast typing.</strong>
            As agents handle more implementation, requirements, system design, and precise task descriptions become a bigger part of the work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Verification stays essential.</strong>
            Tests, code review, observability, and checking that an answer solves the actual problem remain human responsibilities.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Fundamentals still matter.</strong>
            Knowing how software works is how we spot a fictional API, a suspiciously polished mistake, or a bug hiding in line 999.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="disagreement">
          <h3>One open question: how much should agents own?</h3>
          <p>Some of us expect agents to take on most routine coding, testing, and bug-fixing end to end. Others are more cautious: without explainability and human judgment at the important decision points, a fast answer can still be an expensive guess. We agree on the practical part: an agent can help, but a human has to understand and stand behind the result.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="footer-inner">
      <p>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. <span id="current-year"></span> · Group 14</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    (function () {
      const root = document.documentElement;
      const toggle = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
      const icon = toggle.querySelector("[aria-hidden='true']");
      const label = toggle.querySelector(".toggle-label");

      function updateToggle(theme) {
        const isDark = theme === "dark";
        toggle.setAttribute("aria-label", isDark ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
        icon.textContent = isDark ? "☀" : "☾";
        label.textContent = isDark ? "Day mode" : "Night mode";
      }

      updateToggle(root.getAttribute("data-theme"));

      toggle.addEventListener("click", function () {
        const nextTheme = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        root.setAttribute("data-theme", nextTheme);
        updateToggle(nextTheme);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", nextTheme);
        } catch (error) {
          // Theme switching still works for this visit when storage is unavailable.
        }
      });

      document.getElementById("current-year").textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
    }());
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

